Singing and drinking alone, living freely; long songs and sighs, leaving the world to the wind. Inviting brothers and friends, including those on the boat, to gather with wild elders. Playing drinking games and guessing, often passing the cup; dividing tiles and talking, casually passing the time. Cooking shrimp and crabs every day, frying ducks and chickens daily. The foolish wife makes tea carefree, the mountain wife cooks with ease. In the morning, carrying a stick to stir the light waves, in the morning, carrying firewood over the broad rapids. After the rain, wearing a raincoat to catch live carp, before the wind, playing with an axe to cut old pines. Concealing oneself to avoid the world, pretending to be simple and foolish, hiding one's name, pretending to be deaf and dumb.

Brother Li, before I could continue, I would like you to start with a couplet, and I will follow with another one."  
The wind and moon, a drunken mountain wild man; the江湖, a content old wanderer.  
Free from burdens and free-spirited, enjoying life;  
Speak without being heard, living in peace.  
Sleeping soundly in a thatched cottage under the moonlight;  
Covered lightly by a rush cloak in the twilight.  
Forgotten by the world, befriends pines and plum blossoms;  
Friendly to seagulls and herons.  
No thought of gains and losses in the heart;  
No sound of warfare in the ears.  
Enjoying a cup of fine wine at any time;  
Three meals a day of wild vegetables.  
Two bundles of firewood as livelihood;  
A fishing rod as means of survival.  
Lazy, calling the child to sharpen the steel axe;  
Quietly, calling the child to mend the old cloth.  
In spring, loving to see the green willows;  
In winter, happy to see the green reeds.  
In summer, avoiding the heat to make new bamboo;  
In June, basking in the cool to pick tender lotus seeds.  
When the chickens are fat, they are often slaughtered;  
When the crabs are strong, they are promptly cooked.  
In winter, sleeping in the sun, still sleeping;  
In extreme cold, high in the sky, no need to steam.
